  "notes": "History: with the original first-order global-wave-speed Rusanov flux the CI tier FAILED the profile metric (9.82% / 6.29% at nx=200/400 vs the 5% gate); the gate was NOT relaxed. Root cause was diagnosed as the first-order flux's grid-independent numerical viscosity, and src/tensorlbm/shallow_water.py gained a second-order scheme (minmod MUSCL + local-speed HLL + SSP-RK2), after which the same gated levels give 1.17% / 0.83% (front 0.12% / 0.06%, mass drift <= 2.3e-14%), i.e. ~8x and ~7.6x less profile error than the frozen baseline. The legacy flux stays selectable (--scheme rusanov) and its 9.8248% value is pinned by tests/test_shallow_water_muscl2.py as the improvement baseline."
